{"kind":"article","metadata":{"title":"Privacy Manifests","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyTracking"},{"text":" as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":" and lists no tracking domains.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy"},{"type":"text","text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle"},{"type":"text","text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Required-reason